Quoting  Seraphim  <gme6@cornell.edu>:
>impossible to know what context that "2" should be taken in. I'll admit 
>disagree with Jove, but I also disagree with David. IMO the vast majority 
>of deaths from monsters in Nethack are avoidable,

Yes, but there's avoidable and there's avoidable. A death you could avoid
if you checked your inventory very carefully and thought out a clever
strategy is one thing; a death you can avoid by not stepping next to the
water - well, that's a strategy anyone ought to be able to manage.

>so for a good player 
>the "risk" associated with a monster is associated with how much work you 
>have to do to avoid being killed by it. IMO if eels wern't a risk then 
>players wouldn't spend so much time preparing for them.

Do players spend a lot of time preparing for them? It doesn't take me long
to find some rocks.

>So not being killed by Death because you're careful to avoid him doesn't 
>make Death less dangerous, but not being killed by eels because you're 
>careful to avoid them makes eels less dangerous?

Well, there is a difference there; you can't avoid the Plane of Water -
and while you can avoid coming next to eels, your movement is being
dictated by those eels. That's not a case like Astral where there's a 2/3
chance you can completely ignore your least favourite Rider.
